{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS3hhjjhZxdNqN3a2RD5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"After a memory write, the bot should now pay only for the per-athlete part of the prompt, not the whole thing. I tested this offline with a fake client only. There was no API key, so I made no real calls and the token numbers below come from the existing `logs/usage.jsonl`.\n\nThe log showed three separate problems:\n\n1. **One cache marker covered everything.** Any new fact changed the whole cached block, so all ~1100 tokens were written to the cache again.\n2. **The prompt was rebuilt on every tool-loop round.** `save_fact` adds the fact straight into the athlete record, and each round rebuilt the system prompt from it. So the miss happened in round 2 of the *same* message, which is exactly where the log shows `cache_read_input_tokens: 0`.\n3. **Splitting into two markers wouldn't have been enough on its own.** Sonnet 4.5 only caches a marker if everything up to it is at least 1024 tokens. Athlete 77's whole prompt was cached at exactly 1024, so the fixed part (tools plus instructions) is about 950. A marker there would be silently ignored, and every fact write would still re-cache the full prompt.\n\nWhat I changed in `bot.py`:\n- **Two cached blocks.** The first holds the coaching instructions, which are identical for every athlete and day, so they are also shared across athletes. The second holds the volatile part: date, profile, zones, goal, facts and language.\n- **The prompt is built once per message**, before the tool loop. Later rounds now match round 1 exactly and read from the cache. A newly saved fact appears from the next message on, which is what the README already says.\n- **`plan_week` is now always included** instead of only on keywords. That lifts the fixed part to about 1200 tokens, above the minimum, and coaching rule 17 already tells the model to use it for any weekly plan. Keyword filtering is otherwise untouched (`predict_race` still needs a keyword), as NOTES.md asks.\n\n**Decision for you:** the side effect is that the model can call `plan_week` on any message, and each call carries about 250 more tokens, though read from cache at ~10% price. If you'd rather keep the tool set as it was, the alternative is to add 80+ tokens of real, fixed content to the instructions. Without one of the two, the split does nothing on this model.\n\nThe offline check confirmed that rounds 1 and 2 send the same request after a `save_fact`. The instructions block also came out identical for both athletes on different dates. To confirm against the real API, follow the check in `ANSWER.md`: after a fact write, the next message should show about 1200 tokens read from cache and only about 100 newly cached. That file also says which parts of your colleague's note applied (two segments, stable tools, loading all facts, the check itself) and which didn't (their ~780-token fixed part would be too short to cache here).\n\nI didn't commit anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2083,"cache_read_input_tokens":41604,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2083},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"688da107-f88b-4719-8233-0277b1c75f5f","uuid":"468e3413-7da1-4098-b379-231b7ed749df","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:40:19.998Z","request_id":"req_011CgS3hhTsDNXfGoW5K785F"}
